{# Plain-text completion template for a BASE (non-chat) checkpoint.

   Referenced from a geodesic-evals suite as an absolute literal path
   (`chat_template: /abs/path/to/base_completion.jinja`);
   `resolve_chat_template` returns any non-`registry:` string verbatim, so
   this needs no registry entry and no PR to geodesic-environments.

   WHAT IT EMITS: message contents, in order, joined by a blank line.
   Nothing else. No ChatML markers, no role headers, no BOS/EOS, and
   nothing appended for `add_generation_prompt` — a base model must see
   the scenario text exactly as a document, or the loglikelihood/rollout
   comparison against the stock Base checkpoint is measuring template
   compliance instead of the model.

   BOS is deliberately NOT emitted: the /v1/completions endpoint tokenises
   the prompt with add_special_tokens=True, so emitting `bos_token` here
   would double it.

   RENDER CONTRACT (geodesic-environments
   shared_eval_utils/chat_template_utils/render.py:167-178, verified
   2026-08-05 against /projects/a5k/public/repos/geodesic-environments):
     messages              list of {role, content} dicts; roles are
                           system / user / assistant
     add_generation_prompt bool — True when no prefill is configured
     eos_token, bos_token  default "" unless the suite passes them
     plus anything in chat_template_kwargs
   The Jinja env sets trim_blocks=False, lstrip_blocks=False,
   keep_trailing_newline=True, so every literal character below is emitted
   as written. Hence the single-line body (matching nemotron.jinja) and
   the `-%}` on the final tag, which strips this file's trailing newline
   so the prompt ends exactly at the last message's last character. If a
   run wants the model to begin on a fresh line, change that to `%}`.

   PREFILL: when the suite sets a non-empty `prefill`, render.py appends a
   placeholder `{role: assistant, content: "", prefill: <text>}` turn and
   sets add_generation_prompt False; when prefill is "" (this campaign's
   setting) no such turn is appended. `message.get('prefill', '')` is read
   off assistant turns only — which both satisfies `template_accepts_prefill`
   (render.py:80-122 walks the AST for a `prefill` read) and avoids the
   UndefinedError that an unconditional `message['prefill']` would raise on
   a real assistant turn in a multi-turn sample.
   CONTINUATION CUE: a bare, complete scenario paragraph looks like a FINISHED document
   to a base model trained on `</s>`-separated documents — measured on the stock Base:
   every sfm_ind_open rollout emitted exactly one token, `</s>` (completion_tokens=1,
   stop_reason=2), for a 100% excluded run. `continuation_cue` (from the suite's
   chat_template_kwargs, e.g. "\n\nResponse:") is appended after the final message when
   the template is asked for a generation prompt, giving the standard base-model QA
   elicitation frame. Applied identically to baseline/forget_on/forget_off, so
   cross-posture comparisons are unaffected. Default: empty (pure document rendering).
#}{% for message in messages %}{% if not loop.first %}{{ '\n\n' }}{% endif %}{% if message['role'] == 'assistant' %}{{ message.get('prefill', '') }}{{ message.get('content', '') }}{% else %}{{ message['content'] }}{% endif %}{%- endfor %}{% if add_generation_prompt %}{{ continuation_cue | default('') }}{% endif %}
